#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# series

#% text
# `series(e, x, x0, n)` gives the power series of `e` in `x` about the point `x0`, up to the power n of (x - x0).

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The result is a truncated sum followed by an order term `O((x - x0)^(n + 1))` for the terms left out.

#% item
# A pole at `x0` gives negative powers (a Laurent series).

#% item
# The coefficients may hold symbols.

#% item
# `normal` turns a series into its truncated sum, an ordinary expression.

#% item
# An order term in the input, `e + O(x^k)`, limits the result to that order.

#% item
# When there is no power series of the expected form, such as at a branch point of `log` or `sqrt`, or at an essential singularity, the call stays unevaluated.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# The exponential function about 0:

#% cell
series(exp(x), x, 0, 5)
#% output
#= 1 + x + x^2/2 + x^3/6 + x^4/24 + x^5/120 + O(x^6)

#% text
# The sine:

#% cell
series(sin(x), x, 0, 7)
#% output
#= x - x^3/6 + x^5/120 - x^7/5040 + O(x^8)

#% text
# The logarithm about 1:

#% cell
series(log(x), x, 1, 4)
#% output
#= (x - 1) - (x - 1)^2/2 + (x - 1)^3/3 - (x - 1)^4/4 + O((x - 1)^5)

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# A removable singularity:

#% cell
series(sin(x)/x, x, 0, 6)
#% output
#= 1 - x^2/6 + x^4/120 - x^6/5040 + O(x^7)

#% text
# A pole gives negative powers:

#% cell
series(1/sin(x), x, 0, 3)
#% output
#= x^-1 + x/6 + 7*x^3/360 + O(x^4)

#% cell
series(1/(x^2 + x), x, 0, 2)
#% output
#= x^-1 - 1 + x - x^2 + O(x^3)

#% text
# Symbolic coefficients:

#% cell
series(a/(1 - b*x), x, 0, 3)
#% output
#= a + a*b*x + a*b^2*x^2 + a*b^3*x^3 + O(x^4)

#% text
# Compositions and products:

#% cell
series(exp(sin(x)), x, 0, 4)
#% output
#= 1 + x + x^2/2 - x^4/8 + O(x^5)

#% cell
series(tan(x), x, 0, 7)
#% output
#= x + x^3/3 + 2*x^5/15 + 17*x^7/315 + O(x^8)

#% text
# About another point:

#% cell
series(cos(x), x, pi, 3)
#% output
#= -1 + (x - pi)^2/2 + O((x - pi)^4)

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# Approximate a function near a point by its truncated series, and compare:

#% cell
p = normal(series(sin(x), x, 0, 5)); [p /. x -> 0.1, sin(0.1)]
#% output
#= [0.09983341666666667, 0.09983341664682815]

#% text
# Read off a limit from the leading terms:

#% cell
series((1 - cos(x))/x^2, x, 0, 2)
#% output
#= 1/2 - x^2/24 + O(x^3)

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `normal` gives the truncated sum:

#% cell
normal(series(exp(x), x, 0, 3))
#% output
#= 1 + x + (1/6)*x^3 + (1/2)*x^2

#% text
# An order term in the input limits the order of the result:

#% cell
series(cos(x) + O(x^4), x, 0, 6)
#% output
#= 1 - x^2/2 + O(x^4)

#% text
# A polynomial is its own series:

#% cell
series(x^2 + 3x + 1, x, 0, 5)
#% output
#= 1 + 3*x + x^2 + O(x^6)

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# Powers with fractional exponents and logarithms at the point are not expanded:

#% cell
series(log(x), x, 0, 2)
#% output
#= series(log(x), x, 0, 2)

#% cell
series(cos(sqrt(x)), x, 0, 3)
#% output
#= series(cos(x^(1/2)), x, 0, 3)

#% text
# Arithmetic on series is not carried out; take `normal` first:

#% cell
series(exp(x), x, 0, 2)^2
#% output
#= (1 + x + x^2/2 + O(x^3))^2

#% cell
series(normal(series(exp(x), x, 0, 2))^2, x, 0, 2)
#% output
#= 1 + 2*x + 2*x^2 + O(x^3)

#% text
# A substitution into a series keeps the order term; use `normal` first:

#% cell
series(sin(x), x, 0, 3) /. x -> 0.1
#% output
#= 0.1 - 0.1^3/6 + O(0.1^4)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `normal`, `O`, `limit`, `d`, `coefficient`
